description:
IMPLEMENT F1 CLI layer.
FILES: main.rs + dc.rs + resolve.rs

main.rs Command variants (7, top-level kebab-case):
1. ChannelCreate { guild, name, channel_type: Option<ChannelTypeArg>, category: Option<String>, topic: Option<String>, slowmode: Option<u64>, dry_run }
2. ChannelRename { guild, channel, new_name, dry_run }
3. ChannelTopic { guild, channel, topic }
4. ChannelMove { guild, channel, category: Option<String>, position: Option<u32> }
5. ChannelClone { guild, channel, name: Option<String> }
6. ChannelSlowmode { guild, channel, seconds: u64 }
7. ChannelDelete { guild, channel, confirm }
Handlers: dc_channel_create/rename/topic/move/clone/slowmode/delete.

RESOLVERS (resolve.rs):
- resolve_channel_admin(client, guild_id, name) -> Result<Option<String>>: MUST NOT reuse list_channels (filters text-like). Call core get_guild_channels_all(guild_id) -> Vec<crate types::Channel> (Route::GetGuildChannels raw, NO retain filter) — add this small core method in F1a or here. ID-match first, strip '#', case-insensitive exact name, ambiguity -> eprintln list + exit::USAGE (2), not-found -> None -> caller exit::NOT_FOUND (3).
- resolve_category(client, guild_id, name) -> Result<Option<String>>: filter channel_type == 4 from get_guild_channels_all. Same match semantics.

OPTION VALIDATION (exit::USAGE 2):
- --type enum: text|voice|category|announcement|stage|forum -> 0|2|4|5|13|15; invalid -> exit 2 listing valid.
- channel name: 1-100 chars, no '#'. slowmode 0-21600. topic <=1024.
- ChannelMove: requires >=1 of --category/--position else exit 2.

check_confirm helper (dc.rs): fn check_confirm(target_desc, action, id, confirm) -> Option<ExitCode> — emits eprintln 'This will {action} {target} ({id}). Add --confirm to proceed.' returns Some(USAGE) when !confirm else None.

ChannelClone: GET original (get_channel) -> POST create with same type/parent/topic (+ optional --name override).

DESTRUCTIVE GATE: channel-delete requires --confirm (exit 2 absent).

TEST: smoke (no token) — create dry-run exit 0 + 'action'; delete no-confirm exit 2; move no-option exit 2; invalid --type exit 2; name validation. Unit — resolve_channel_admin strip/match/ambiguity.

ACCEPTANCE: 7 commands work; delete gated; move no-option exit 2; invalid --type exit 2; F1b bead closed.

IMPLEMENT F2 MCP layer.
FILE: crates/discord-mcp/src/server.rs
New #[tool]s (6) — all call ApiClient core (F2a), never Route directly; params schemars derives; return serde_json::to_string; errors .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?:
1. list_roles(guild_id, limit?) -> JSON Vec<Role>
2. create_role(guild_id, name, color?: String('#RRGGBB'), permissions?: Vec<String>, mentionable?: bool, hoist?: bool) -> JSON Role. Parse color/permissions via F2a helpers.
3. edit_role(guild_id, role_id, name?, color?, permissions?, mentionable?, hoist?) -> JSON Role
4. delete_role(guild_id, role_id, confirm) -> advisory confirm: if !confirm Err('... requires confirm: true'). JSON {deleted:true}
5. assign_role(guild_id, user_id, role_id) -> JSON {assigned:true}
6. remove_role(guild_id, user_id, role_id) -> JSON {removed:true}

ACCEPTANCE: 6 tools registered; delete gated confirm:true; F2c bead closed.
